! ============================================================
! Synthetic firewall policy — Water Treatment OT reference topology (Rev D)
! Vendor syntax: Cisco ASA extended ACL (single syntax, dataset v1)
! Enforcement point: the one inline appliance in the Level 3.5 DMZ,
! deployed as a /32 host-routed Zero Trust Branch style appliance —
! every device on every VLAN below routes back to this appliance,
! so its policy is authoritative for BOTH north-south (IT<->OT) and
! east-west (area<->area) traffic. See perimeter_ngfw_only.acl for
! the deployment shape where east-west is out of this device's scope.
!
! Address scheme (all RFC1918, synthetic):
!   L4  Enterprise IT         10.4.0.0/16
!   DMZ VLAN 40                10.40.0.0/24
!     .11 historian mirror | .12 patch/AV proxy | .13 remote access broker
!   L3  VLAN 30 (site ops)     10.30.0.0/24
!     .10 SCADA server | .11 OT historian | .12 eng workstation | .13 alarm/AD-DNS
!   L2-1 VLAN 12 Intake        10.12.0.0/24   (.10 HMI-1 / .11 PLC-1)
!   L2-1 VLAN 13 Filtration    10.13.0.0/24   (.10 HMI-2 / .11 PLC-2)
!   L2-1 VLAN 14 Disinfection  10.14.0.0/24   (.10 HMI-3 / .11 PLC-3)
!   L2-1 VLAN 15 Distribution  10.15.0.0/24   (.10 HMI-4 / .11 PLC-4)
!   L1  SIS enclave (diode)    10.101.1.5 — not part of this ACL; bridged
!       to 10.30.0.11 by a one-way hardware data diode, no routable path,
!       not policy enforced. Compliance for this boundary is checked
!       against traffic evidence direction only (see Section 4.3 clause 3).
! ============================================================

! --- IT (L4) -> DMZ (L3.5) : the only path IT has toward OT ---
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 host 10.40.0.11 eq 443
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 host 10.40.0.12 eq 443
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 host 10.40.0.13 eq 443
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.4.0.0 255.255.0.0 any log

! --- DMZ (L3.5) -> Site Ops (L3) : specific brokered paths only ---
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.11 host 10.40.0.11 eq 1433
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.12 host 10.30.0.10 eq 443
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.12 host 10.30.0.11 eq 443
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.12 host 10.30.0.12 eq 443
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.40.0.13 host 10.30.0.12 eq 3389
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.40.0.0 255.255.255.0 any log

! --- Site Ops (L3) -> Area segments (L2-1) : SCADA polling + eng access ---
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.12.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.13.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.14.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.10 10.15.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.12.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.13.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.14.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended permit tcp host 10.30.0.12 10.15.0.0 255.255.255.0 eq 502

! --- Area (L2-1) <-> Area (L2-1) : deny by default, host-routed makes this checkable ---
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.12.0.0 255.255.255.0 10.13.0.0 255.255.255.0 log
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.12.0.0 255.255.255.0 10.14.0.0 255.255.255.0 log
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.12.0.0 255.255.255.0 10.15.0.0 255.255.255.0 log
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.13.0.0 255.255.255.0 10.14.0.0 255.255.255.0 log
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.13.0.0 255.255.255.0 10.15.0.0 255.255.255.0 log
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip 10.14.0.0 255.255.255.0 10.15.0.0 255.255.255.0 log

! --- Default deny ---
access-list OT-ENFORCE extended deny ip any any log
